{
  peppy_schema: "contract/v1",
  manifest: {
    name: "limb_motion",
    tag: "v1",
    description: [
      "Discrete, planned moves of the limbs of a multi-arm manipulator: a joint-space arm move, a joint-space path of one or more arms, a Cartesian arm move, and a gripper move, each addressing its limbs by names from the implementer's fixed set.",
      "Each goal is planned and executed by the implementer and returns a result; they are distinct from the streamed setpoints on the joint_link / gripper_link / pose_link pairings.",
      "Every Cartesian pose, commanded or reported, is the gripper's grasp point, in the robot frame, position in meters and orientation as a unit quaternion [x, y, z, w]. On a gripper whose jaws close symmetrically, it is on the jaw closing axis midway between the pads. The SO-101 gripper has one moving jaw, so the midpoint of its pads moves with the opening. Thus, the SO-101 takes and reports a fixed point near its jaws.",
      "The robot frame is fixed to the robot's base: its origin is the point the base stands on, +X points the way the robot faces, +Y to its left and +Z up. It moves with the robot, and it is not a frame of the room or of a simulated world.",
      "Every move settles from the planned end of its motion on, and its caller's settle_timeout_s bounds how long that may take. An arm move completes as soon as the arm stands within the tolerance the caller names, and fails if it does not by the timeout. A gripper move completes as soon as the jaws stand still, on the target or stopped short of it by what they hold, and at the timeout it completes wherever they stand: a grasp is expected to stop short, so a gripper move never fails on its settle. Any move ends early when its caller cancels it or the stop service ends every move in flight, whoever started them. check_arm_move asks whether a Cartesian move has a plan, and moves nothing.",
      "move_arm_joints, execute_joint_path, move_arm and move_gripper have the mark `moves_robot`, and stop and check_arm_move have no mark: each MCP server, `peppy node call` and each lease holder asks the daemon (`robot_leases.check_move`) whether it may move the robot before it calls a move, so a stop never waits for a lease.",
      "Every tolerance a goal carries is a positive number in its unit, and every duration and timeout a number of seconds from 0 to 60: an arm move with a timeout of 0 fails at its planned end unless the arm already stands within tolerance. A goal that names other values is refused with `rejected`.",
      "A move goal is refused with `leader_streaming` while a leader streams its limb, and with `precondition_failed` while the limb executes another move. A leader is a robot commander, such as a leader arm or the browser panel, or the headset. An arm move that does not settle by its timeout fails with `timeout`, and the message says how far the arm still stands from the target and how long after the planned end. A move fails with `resource_unavailable` when its limb stops answering, and with `attempt_failed` when it cannot go on for another reason. A cancelled goal gives the reason of the cancel and its result, measured when the move ended. A failed goal gives no result.",
      "The positions and orientations in the robot frame have the mark `robot_frame` (marks.json5). The workflow side reads it: a workflow passes a position or an orientation only from a field with this mark of a result or an observation of the same role, never as a literal.",
    ],
  },
  failure_kinds: {
    unreachable: "No plan to the target, or a path the collision guard would hold short",
    leader_streaming: "A leader streams a limb of the goal",
  },
  interfaces: {
    actions: [
      {
        name: "move_arm_joints",
        description: "Move one arm to a joint configuration, on a trajectory that the implementer plans, and wait until each measured joint settles within its tolerance of its target. A target joint up to 0.001 rad outside its limits runs at the limit, so a measured position sent back as a target runs; one farther out is refused with `rejected`, and the message names the joint, its position and its limits. A move the joint limits cannot run within 60 s fails with rejected before the arm moves, and the message gives its time. The action gives no feedback. The result gives the measured joint positions when the action ended.",
        goal_service: {
          request_message_format: {
            arm_name: { $type: "string", $description: "Which arm, named from the implementer's fixed set of limb names (e.g. \"left_arm\"). An unknown name is refused with `rejected`." },
            joint_positions: { $type: "array", $items: "f64", $description: "Target joint positions (rad), one per joint of the arm in its fixed joint order." },
            duration_s: { $type: "f64", $description: "Requested trajectory duration (s), up to 60; floored at the duration the implementer's joint limits allow. 0 = fastest." },
            settle_tolerances_rad: { $type: "array", $items: "f64", $description: "The move completes once, at or after the planned end of the trajectory, each measured joint stands within its tolerance (rad) of its target: one value per joint of the arm, in its fixed joint order." },
            settle_timeout_s: { $type: "f64", $description: "How long (s) after the planned end the joints may still stand outside their tolerances before the move fails. The arm then holds where it stands either way: on the target, or where the implementer's collision guard held it short." },
          },
        },
        result_service: {
          response_message_format: {
            final_joint_positions: { $type: "array", $items: "f64", $description: "Measured joint positions (rad) when the action ended, one per joint of the arm in its fixed joint order." },
            action_time: { $type: "f64", $description: "Wall-clock duration of the action (s)." },
          },
        },
        failure_kinds: ["leader_streaming"],
        marks: ["moves_robot"],
      },
      {
        name: "execute_joint_path",
        description: "Moves arms smoothly through joint waypoints, on one timing: each arm runs in straight joint-space legs from where it measures when the move starts (the implementer moves its command there) toward each of its waypoints in turn, and the arms pass their k-th waypoints together. Each inner corner is cut by the largest circular arc, tangent to both legs, whose midpoint lies at most 0.1 from the corner (Euclidean, over the joints of every arm) and whose tangent points lie at most half of each leg from it: the arms pass near the inner waypoints and reach the last ones. The arms stop at their last waypoints, where the path turns back on itself (the cosine of the angle between one leg and the next is -0.99999 or less, a turn of about 179.74 degrees), and where each arm's waypoint lies within 0.001 of its waypoint before in every joint. Joint positions are in rad, or m for a prismatic joint, each arm's in its joint order of limb_state. Where it models the robot's body, the implementer checks the whole path against it, at points at most 0.01 rad apart, before any arm moves, and a path its guard would hold short at one of them fails with unreachable. An unknown or repeated arm name, arms with different numbers of waypoints, a waypoint whose joint lies more than 0.001 rad outside its limits (one closer runs at the limit; the message names the waypoint, the joint, its position and its limits), and an array whose length does not match its arm's joints are refused with rejected; a path the joint limits cannot run within 60 s fails with rejected before any arm moves, and the message gives its time. The message of a precondition_failed names its cause.",
        goal_service: {
          request_message_format: {
            arms: {
              $type: "array",
              $description: "The arms to move, at least one, each with its own waypoints.",
              $items: {
                $type: "object",
                arm_name: { $type: "string", $description: "The limb name (e.g. \"left_arm\")." },
                waypoints: {
                  $type: "array",
                  $description: "The positions to pass through, at least one; every arm has as many.",
                  $items: {
                    $type: "object",
                    joint_positions: { $type: "array", $items: "f64" },
                  },
                },
                expected_start_joint_positions: { $type: "array", $items: "f64", $description: "If not empty, the move fails with precondition_failed before any arm moves unless each of the arm's measured joints stands within the implementer's start tolerance of its value here. Pass the arm's start_joint_positions of a plan." },
                settle_tolerances_rad: { $type: "array", $items: "f64", $description: "The move completes once, at or after its planned end, the arms have run the path to its end and each measured joint of the arm stands within its tolerance (above 0) of the arm's last waypoint; one per joint." },
              },
            },
            duration_s: { $type: "f64", $description: "Requested duration of the whole path (s), up to 60; floored at the duration the joint limits allow. 0 = fastest." },
            settle_timeout_s: { $type: "f64", $description: "How long (s, 0 to 60) after the planned end the joints may stand outside their tolerances before the move fails. The arms then hold where they stand either way: at their last waypoints, or where the implementer's collision guard held them short." },
          },
        },
        result_service: {
          response_message_format: {
            arms: {
              $type: "array",
              $description: "Each arm's measured joint positions when the move ended, in the order of the goal's arms.",
              $items: {
                $type: "object",
                arm_name: "string",
                final_joint_positions: { $type: "array", $items: "f64" },
              },
            },
            action_time: { $type: "f64", $description: "Wall-clock duration of the action (s)." },
          },
        },
        failure_kinds: ["unreachable", "leader_streaming"],
        marks: ["moves_robot"],
      },
      {
        name: "move_arm",
        description: "Move the grasp point of one arm to a pose in the robot frame, or to a position with no particular orientation, on a trajectory that the implementer plans, and wait until the measured grasp point settles there. The grasp point travels on a straight line from where it is commanded now, and the plan ends within 1 mm and 0.01 rad of the goal, the default of MoveIt's Cartesian precision. A goal that no such line reaches fails with `unreachable`; a joint path planned for the pose reaches what a line does not, within the slack the planner's goal names. An arm with fewer than six actuated joints ends on few orientations exactly, so it reaches most goals with orientation absent. A line the joint limits cannot run within 60 s fails with `rejected`. The settle tolerances judge arrival, and no plan reads them: the move completes once, at or after the planned end of the trajectory, the measured grasp point stands within them of the commanded goal, so a tolerance tighter than the plan's precision can fail with `timeout`. The action gives no feedback. The result gives the measured grasp-point pose when the action ended.",
        goal_service: {
          request_message_format: {
            arm_name: { $type: "string", $description: "Which arm, named from the implementer's fixed set of limb names (e.g. \"left_arm\"). An unknown name is refused with `rejected`." },
            position: { $type: "array", $items: "f64", $length: 3, $marks: ["robot_frame"], $description: "Target grasp-point position, robot frame: x, y, z (m)." },
            orientation: { $type: "array", $items: "f64", $length: 4, $optional: true, $marks: ["robot_frame"], $description: "Target grasp-point orientation, quaternion [x, y, z, w]. Absent names no orientation: the grasp point aims to keep the turn it starts with. An arm with six or more joints keeps it exactly or has no line to the position; one with fewer ends as near it as its joints allow." },
            duration_s: { $type: "f64", $description: "Requested trajectory duration (s), up to 60; floored at the duration the implementer's joint limits allow. 0 = fastest." },
            settle_position_tolerance_m: { $type: "f64", $description: "Position settle tolerance (m): the Euclidean distance between the measured and commanded grasp-point positions." },
            settle_orientation_tolerance_rad: { $type: "f64", $description: "Orientation settle tolerance (rad): the geodesic angle between the measured orientation and the commanded one, the goal's or, with orientation absent, where the plan ends." },
            settle_timeout_s: { $type: "f64", $description: "How long (s) after the planned end the grasp point may still stand outside the settle tolerances before the move fails. The arm then holds where it stands either way: on the target, or where the implementer's collision guard held it short." },
          },
        },
        result_service: {
          response_message_format: {
            final_position: { $type: "array", $items: "f64", $length: 3, $marks: ["robot_frame"], $description: "Measured grasp-point position when the action ended: x, y, z (m)." },
            final_orientation: { $type: "array", $items: "f64", $length: 4, $marks: ["robot_frame"], $description: "Measured grasp-point orientation, quaternion [x, y, z, w]." },
            action_time: { $type: "f64", $description: "Wall-clock duration of the action (s)." },
          },
        },
        failure_kinds: ["unreachable", "leader_streaming"],
        marks: ["moves_robot"],
      },
      {
        name: "move_gripper",
        description: "Drive one gripper to an opening and wait until its jaws stand still. From the planned end of the commanded travel on, the move completes as soon as the measured opening has stood still: every opening the gripper reported over 0.25 s lies within 0.01 of full jaw travel of the others. Jaws an object or the effort cap stops short of the target stand still there, and complete the move too. settle_timeout_s after the planned end the move completes wherever the jaws stand. The action gives no feedback. The result tells whether the jaws stood still before the timeout, and gives the measured opening when the move ended.",
        goal_service: {
          request_message_format: {
            gripper_name: { $type: "string", $description: "Which gripper, named from the implementer's fixed set of gripper names (e.g. \"left_gripper\"). An unknown name is refused with `rejected`." },
            opening: { $type: "f64", $description: "Target opening as a fraction of full jaw travel: 0 = closed, 1 = fully open." },
            max_effort: { $type: "f64", $description: "Maximum effort toward the target (magnitude, in the gripper's effort unit). 0 = no preference; the implementer's configured ceiling applies." },
            settle_timeout_s: { $type: "f64", $description: "The longest (s) the move waits for the jaws to stand still, from the planned end of the commanded travel on: the tick the commanded opening, ramping to the target at the implementer's opening rate, comes to rest on the target or where the implementer's collision guard holds it." },
          },
        },
        result_service: {
          response_message_format: {
            settled: { $type: "bool", $description: "True when the jaws stood still before the settle timeout; false when the move completed at the timeout." },
            final_opening: { $type: "f64", $description: "Measured opening fraction when the move ended: the target, the opening where an object or the effort cap stopped the jaws, or wherever they stood at the settle timeout. The caller judges a grasp from it." },
            action_time: { $type: "f64", $description: "Wall-clock duration of the action (s)." },
          },
        },
        failure_kinds: ["leader_streaming"],
        marks: ["moves_robot"],
      },
    ],
    services: [
      {
        name: "stop",
        description: "End every planned move in flight on this robot, whoever started it: the moves of this contract and the posture moves of the same implementer. Each limb holds where it is commanded, as after a cancel, and each goal that the stop ends is cancelled, with a reason that names the stop and the reason of the stop request. A goal that arrives after the stop runs as usual. Setpoints streamed on a pairing are not stopped. The stop gives an error reply, with `attempt_failed`, only when the stop itself cannot be carried out.",
        request_message_format: {
          reason: { $type: "string", $description: "Why the moves are stopped, carried into the reason of each goal the stop ends. Empty is accepted." },
        },
        response_message_format: {
          stopped: { $type: "array", $items: "string", $description: "The limbs whose move was stopped, by their limb names; empty when nothing moved, as for a stop with nothing in flight." },
        },
      },
      {
        name: "check_arm_move",
        description: "Tell whether a move_arm goal with these fields has a plan from where the arm is commanded now, without moving it. The request holds the fields of the move_arm goal that decide whether it has a plan, with the same meaning. It checks what move_arm checks before it moves, and no more: it does not check collisions with the robot itself or with what stands around it. A request that move_arm would refuse gets an error reply with the kind of that refusal: `rejected` for an unknown arm or a field that move_arm does not take, `precondition_failed` while the arm executes a move, which the check does not disturb, and `leader_streaming` while a leader streams the arm.",
        request_message_format: {
          arm_name: "string",
          position: { $type: "array", $items: "f64", $length: 3, $marks: ["robot_frame"] },
          orientation: { $type: "array", $items: "f64", $length: 4, $optional: true, $marks: ["robot_frame"], $description: "As for move_arm: absent names no orientation." },
          duration_s: "f64",
        },
        response_message_format: {
          reachable: { $type: "bool", $description: "True when a plan exists." },
          reason: { $type: "string", $description: "Why no plan exists, in the words that the move_arm failure gives; empty when reachable." },
          duration_s: { $type: "f64", $description: "The time the move would take (s); 0 when not reachable." },
        },
        failure_kinds: ["leader_streaming"],
      },
    ],
  },
}
